    "question_text": "The periodic table consists of 18 groups. An isotope of copper, on bombardment with protons, undergoes a nuclear reaction yielding element $X$ as shown below. To which group, element $X$ belongs in the periodic table?\r\n\r\n${ }_{29}^{63} \\mathrm{Cu}+{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H} \\rightarrow 6_{0}^{1} n+{ }_{2}^{4} \\alpha+2{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H}+\\mathrm{X}$",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [],
    "correct_answer": "8",
    "solution_text": "${ }_{29}^{63} \\mathrm{Cu}+{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H} \\rightarrow 6{ }_{0}^{1} n+{ }_{2}^{4} \\mathrm{He}+2{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H}+{ }_{Z}^{A} X$\r\n\r\nBalancing the atomic mass and atomic number\r\n\r\n$63+1=(6 \\times 1)+4+2+A \\Rightarrow A=52$\r\n\r\n$29+1=(6 \\times 0)+2+2+Z \\Rightarrow Z=26$\r\n\r\nThus ${ }_{Z}^{A} X={ }_{26}^{52} X$ or ${ }_{26}^{52} \\mathrm{Fe}$\r\n\r\nHence, $X$ belongs to group 8 in the periodic table.",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Modern periodic table"
  },
  {
    "question_id": "6a0be51644d287c9361e5cd2",
    "type": "multipleCorrect",
    "difficulty_level": 2,
    "syllabus_category": "noChange",
